# CODEOWNERS — separation of duties for the governance control plane.
#
# Changes to the audit POLICY, the detection ENGINE, the CI GATE, and the
# SECURITY baseline must be reviewed by the governance/security owners below —
# not by the same author who edits a skill in the same merge request. This is
# the human half of "the gate cannot weaken itself"; the engine half is the
# severity floor in scripts/agent_audit.py.
#
# Replace @skill-governance-owners with your real GitLab/GitHub group or
# usernames (same as the REPLACE-ME sentinels elsewhere in the repo).
#
# IMPORTANT: a CODEOWNERS file only ENFORCES review when branch protection is
# configured to require code-owner approval. In GitLab: Settings → Repository →
# Protected branches → "Require approval from Code Owners" on the default
# branch. Without that project setting, this file is advisory only.

# --- Audit policy and rule catalog (who can change the standards) ---
/references/agent-audit-rules.json          @skill-governance-owners
/references/agent-audit-config.example.json  @skill-governance-owners

# --- Suppression list + security data (who can SILENCE a finding) ---
# audit-ignore.json suppresses findings; gating it prevents an MR author from
# self-approving the silencing of their own security finding. The confusables
# table and audit-config glob are control-plane data the engine trusts.
/references/audit-ignore.json               @skill-governance-owners
/references/unicode-confusables.json        @skill-governance-owners
/references/audit-config.*.json             @skill-governance-owners

# --- Deterministic engine + read-only MCP wrapper ---
/scripts/agent_audit.py                     @skill-governance-owners
/scripts/agent_governance_mcp.py            @skill-governance-owners

# --- CI gate templates (who can change enforcement) ---
/references/ci/gitlab-ci.yml                @skill-governance-owners
/references/ci/github-pr.yml                @skill-governance-owners

# --- Security baseline + the checks reference ---
/skills/library-audit/references/security-spec.md  @skill-governance-owners
/docs/checks-reference.md                   @skill-governance-owners

# --- Shipped runtime security controls (execute on user machines) ---
# The secret-guard hook ships into users' .claude/settings.json as a PreToolUse
# hook and runs automatically on every Bash tool call — weakening it in an
# ordinary MR would silently disable a fleet-wide control. audit.sh P18
# machine-checks this entry stays present.
/skills/integration-init/assets/secret-guard-hook.py  @skill-governance-owners

# --- The toolkit's OWN enforcement plane (the gate cannot weaken itself) ---
# Without code-owner review here, an author could disable the self-CI gate,
# rewrite the release/version machinery, or neuter the MR poster in the SAME
# merge request that ships a skill — silently weakening the gate meant to review
# that very change. audit.sh P18 machine-checks this list stays covered.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml                   @skill-governance-owners
/scripts/audit.sh                           @skill-governance-owners
/scripts/sync_version.py                    @skill-governance-owners
/scripts/post_mr_comment.py                 @skill-governance-owners
/VERSION                                    @skill-governance-owners
